            <ArticleTitle>A small Askin's tumor presenting with early onset of chest pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>112</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1186/s12957-015-0506-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most primitive neuroectodermal tumor of the chest wall destroy the rib, chest wall muscles, diaphragm, and lung or extend into the spinal compartment, resulting in a large-sized tumor and symptoms. In contrast, we recently encountered a rare case of Askin's tumor presenting with early-onset chest pain despite the small size. After resection of the tumor and adjuvant chemotherapy, the patient remains disease-free over 3 years of follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
